102,0$Lamellae pallid, then pale butterscotch to dingy orange white; pileus 20-40 mm in diameter, butterscotch or buff, fading to orange white or off-white, disc darker for some time, grayish orange or pale orange; odor and taste not distinctive .$C. coniferophila (pg. 177)
102,0$Lamellae lavender, then pale gray flushed with pink, fading to buff pink or buff; pileus10-55(-115) mm in diameter, dark brown, fading to brown, light brown, brownish orange, grayish orange, disc often darker; odor absent, fungoid, or faintly sweet, sometimes farinaceous in age; taste mild, slightly metallic, or fungoid$C. tarda var. tarda (pg. 88)
103,104$Lamellae brown, gray, brownish gray, or brownish orange in moist basidiocarp .$
